{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>תִּשְׁמְטֶנָּה וּנְטַשְׁתָּהּ</b> (you shall let it rest and abandon it). תִּשְׁמְטֶנָּה — from work; וּנְטַשְׁתָּהּ — from gathering food after the time of בִּעוּר (gleaning). Another interpretation: תִּשְׁמְטֶנָּה — from complete work, such as plowing and sowing, and וּנְטַשְׁתָּהּ — from fertilizing and hoeing. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 23:11). But it is not correct, for we were prohibited by the Torah only concerning plowing and sowing; but one who hoes or fertilizes, and even one who weeds or hoes or prunes or performs any other work of the ground, is not forbidden by Torah law. Thus they raised the question at the beginning of tractate Moed Katan (3a), in the chapter Mashkin: plowing and sowing the Merciful One prohibited, but their derivatives the Merciful One did not prohibit, and all of them are by rabbinic law, and the verse is merely an asmakhta (a scriptural hook). Likewise, the law of בִּעוּר is not derived from this verse. And Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 23:11), 'תִּשְׁמְטֶנָּה — let every owner withdraw his hand; וּנְטַשְׁתָּהּ — that you shall not sow your land.' But this is nothing at all. Rather, the verse is attached to the first clause: it said <b>שֵׁשׁ שָׁנִים תִּזְרַע</b> (six years you shall sow) and you may gather the produce, <b>וְהַשְּׁבִיעִית תִּשְׁמְטֶנָּה</b> (and the seventh you shall let it rest) — that you shall not sow your land, <b>וּנְטַשְׁתָּהּ</b> (and abandon it) — that you shall not gather its produce, but rather leave it, <b>וְאָכְלוּ אֶבְיוֹנֵי עַמֶּךָ</b> (and the poor of your people shall eat) — and the beasts of the field shall eat the fruit of the tree and the produce of the vineyard; and likewise, 'and they abandoned the seventh year' (Nehemiah 10:32)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "In the phrase 'one who hoes or fertilizes, and even one who weeds or hoes,' the root מכש appears to recur; I have translated each occurrence literally as it stands in the text."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:18:33.707764163Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}